> Fill in the <PLACEHOLDERS> for your product. Keep `DESIGN-DECISIONS-LOG.md` alongside it.

## RULE #0 — Fidelity first (process; non-negotiable)
**When building any mockup/variation on top of designs that already exist for this product,
FIRST recreate the previously-agreed-upon design with 100% fidelity — exact markup, classes,
structure, fields, spacing, fonts and behavior — by reading the real source file and copying
it. Only then add the new feature on top.** Never ship a simplified, approximate, or
"lighter" version of an existing surface. If unsure how something currently looks, open the
source and match it — do not guess. Approximations waste time and are unacceptable.

## RULE #1 — Log every design decision (process; non-negotiable)
**Every decision made in a session — a change, rename, restyle, behavior rule, or new
convention — MUST be recorded in `DESIGN-DECISIONS-LOG.md` at the project root**, the moment
it's agreed, with: date, what changed (before → after), the exact spec (values/markup), and
**every surface/file it affects** (so it can be applied retroactively to older modules). The
log is the single source of truth for cross-cutting changes; when starting work, read it and
bring stale surfaces up to date. If a decision isn't in the log, it's considered lost.

